card c05
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Isotope does not mean radioactive
figure: isotope-stability
figure_at: 2

body:
    Many people hear 'isotope' and think 'radioactive', but isotope only means a version of an element. Carbon-12 and carbon-13 are stable, and most of the atoms around you are stable isotopes. Carbon-14 is one of the few that is not.

